# Tech stack

- TypeScript (strict), React 19, and Vite 8.
- Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, with CSS-first tokens and scoped styles.
- `lucide-react` for interface icons.
- React state/refs plus profile-specific `localStorage` caches; no external store.
- Vitest for unit tests.
- `vite-plugin-pwa` and `sharp` for the installable app and icons.
- Vercel API function at `api/hana-sync.ts`.
- Postgres through `@neondatabase/serverless`; `DATABASE_URL` or `POSTGRES_URL`.

Do not assume shadcn/ui, Zustand, Sonner, Framer Motion, canvas-confetti, or
date-fns. They are not installed.

## Layout

- `src/App.tsx` — home, Hana controller, top-level view state.
- `src/features/cramble/CrambleExperience.tsx` — isolated Cramble controller.
- `src/lib/hanaGame.ts` — pure shared cadence/quest/date/reward/state functions.
- `src/lib/customHabits.ts` — custom-habit validation and definition creation.
- `src/components/AddHabitDialog.tsx` — shared accessible creation UI.
- `src/lib/hanaCloudSync.ts` — profile-aware payload creation.
- `src/lib/hanaRemoteState.ts` — profile-aware remote helpers.
- `src/data/` — separate Hana and Cramble catalogs.
- `src/pages/` — screen components.
- `src/styles/globals.css` — Tailwind entry, tokens, variants, reward scenes.
- `api/hana-sync.ts` — shared profile-partitioned database endpoint.

## Rules

- Keep business logic in pure `lib/` functions rather than page components.
- Keep daily, exact-weekday, `periodTarget`, and legacy-quota calculations in
  `hanaGame.ts` with boundary tests; do not duplicate cadence math in profile
  controllers.
- Keep counted custom records in `habitOccurrences`, separate from legacy
  boolean `dailyCompletions`. Period targets allow same-day repetition, award
  once only at the full target, and support one-at-a-time undo.
- Resolve built-in and persisted custom definitions through `getQuestCatalog()`
  before planning, reward, sync, or stats work.
- Preserve separate cache keys, catalogs, and save queues for both profiles.
- Pass the profile id and quest catalog explicitly at generic sync boundaries.
- Prefer zero new dependencies; justify and document additions.
- Keep API changes compatible with Vercel and validate profile ownership.
- Full details: `docs/ai/architecture.md` and `docs/ai/database-sync.md`.
